==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Submarine_periscope.jpg|thumb|right|Naval officer using a periscope]]

===Etymology===
From {{confix|en|peri|scope}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɛɹɪskəʊp/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-periscope.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A form of viewing device that allows the viewer to see things at a different height level and usually with minimal visibility.
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Land That Time Forgot||IV|passage=The waters grew suddenly lighter, and my spirits rose accordingly. I shouted down to those below that I saw daylight ahead, and a great shout of thanksgiving reverberated through the ship. A moment later we emerged into sunlit water, and immediately I raised the '''periscope''' and looked about me upon the strangest landscape I had ever seen.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A general or comprehensive view.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1885|journal=Transactions of the Michigan State Medical Society|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=t69XAAAAMAAJ|page=55|passage={{...}} will show it not only enlarging the '''periscope''' of knowledge, but contributing to the amelioration of the condition of unfortunate and suffering humanity {{...}}}}

