===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To rise and [[peer]] around, in the manner of a periscope.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1951|title=National Geographic Magazine: Volume 99
|passage=Thousands of ungainly black-beaked heads would '''periscope''' and freeze in the direction of the approaching intruder.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1987|title=Field & Stream March 1987
|passage=The second summer I had a great deal of interest but weeks passed before I worked up the nerve to approach her, the confidence finally gained when I caught a queen snake that '''periscoped''' within reach, one of the last I ever saw swimming in Cross Creek.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=Doug Stamm|title=The Springs of Florida|page=99
|passage=Areas of barren sand are likely spots to look for its [the turtle's] '''periscoping''' head. Its fondness for the bottom is equally matched by its ability to quickly disappear and tunnel into it.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Jim Moran|title=The Sentinel: A Wildfire Story|page=236
|passage=Her black and white head suddenly popped out from under the covers and '''periscoped''' around.}}

